# Where we are: the map and the table of where the board's statements came from.

map-meta-title = Where we are · 333
map-meta-description = A world map of the 333 nodes that left a signed address at the meeting point in the last two epochs, rounded to whole degrees, with Tor counted separately.

map-heading = Where we are
map-lede = Every node that says where it can be reached leaves that statement at <a href="{ $base }/333">the333.dev/333</a>, and the request carrying it arrives from somewhere. This is that, counted. It is not a census: a node that was handed an invitation and never came here is not in it, and neither is one that told this place nothing.
map-tor = A node reachable through Tor is counted as Tor and placed in no country. The request that carried its statement came from an ordinary address like everybody else&#8217;s, and that address is the one thing an onion address exists to withhold, so it is dropped here rather than stored.
map-where = Where
map-saying = Saying
map-rounding = Positions are rounded to whole degrees, which is about a hundred kilometres. The board holds a statement for two epochs and then forgets it, so this shows who has spoken recently rather than who exists.
map-picture = A world map with a mark where each node is
